--- what this closure does NOT claim (§11.4.6) ---
It does NOT rest on "no incidents since 2026-08-19". Six days have elapsed with no
new forced-logout incident document (the series stops at the 6th, and the 7th IS
BOB-126), but absence of a report is not proof of absence of an event — §11.4.201(6).
The load-bearing evidence is the root-cause fix being present and gated, plus the
established family precedent, NOT a quiet interval.

--- THE HALF THAT DOES NOT CLOSE HERE ---
BOB-120's title names TWO things: the incident, and a "preventive-timer-inside-
user-slice architectural gap". Only the incident closes. The architectural gap is
carried by BOB-121 ("External watchdog for the forced-logout architectural gap",
status: Ready for testing), which remains OPEN. This is recorded explicitly so the
gap is transferred, never absorbed — closing BOB-120 without saying this would
silently retire an unfixed architectural concern along with a fixed incident.
